NOTES AND QUESTIONS ON PLEADING BY PLAINTIFFS UNDER THE RULES
As noted above, the federal courts never adopted code pleading. Instead, with the adoption of the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure in 1938, federal civil practice shifted from procedures that were still grounded in common law and equity procedure to their modern form. And as also noted above, many characteristics of pleading under the Rules reflect a conscious rejection of prior systems.

